# Riff architecture

- `riff/core/` must not import `gi` (secrets may lazy-import optionally).
- Network, disk, and yt-dlp work belong on worker threads. Touch GTK only via `GLib.idle_add` or `riff.util.run_async`.
- Never pass untrusted strings to a shell.
- Secrets go through `riff.core.secrets`, not `settings.json`.
- Prefer extending existing modules under `riff/core/` and `riff/ui/` over new parallel layers.
